	d͡ʒ > j, occasionally ɟ or d͡ʒ in educated speech
	θ ð ðˤ > t d dˤ
	q > ɡ
	a:[+ long] > e:[+ long] / in Form VI (tafā‘ala) verbs, though these apparently coexist with forms having the
				original vowel as well, with semantic distinctions
	a:[+ long] > æ:[+ long] / when not near emphatics
	# Epenthesis (it seems i is preferred) breaking up final consonant clusters
	V:[- long] > ∅ / #C_C, in some words